# Nougat extraction — STUB

**Status:** placeholder. Full Nougat (Meta AI PDF-to-mathematical-markdown)
extraction of Parrish et al. PRL 122, 230401 (2019) / arXiv:1901.01234 was
**not** run in this backfill.

## Why

- The paper's equations (Eq. 4, 5, 6, 8 in particular) and the supplemental
  dipole two-body formula were transcribed **manually** from the PDF and
  arXiv source during the primary replication (see `report/REPORT.md` §1 and
  §3).
- The paper's TeraChem monomer numbers and BChl-a XYZ geometry are in a
  supplemental data packet **absent from the arXiv source**, so a Nougat
  extraction of the arXiv PDF would not surface the numerical data that was
  most missing.
- The primary replication is a from-scratch NumPy/SciPy implementation, not a
  code-lift from the paper — so no code lives inside the paper PDF to extract.

## What a real extraction would deliver

A full Nougat pass over `arXiv:1901.01234v2` would produce a Markdown / MathJax
rendering of:

- Main-text equations (Eq. 1–8), matching what was transcribed by hand.
- The supplemental dipole/transition-dipole two-body formula and the CIS
  reference construction.
- Figure captions (LH2 ring geometry, H-aggregate stack geometry, convergence
  plot).
- References list (~30 entries, mostly VQE and multi-state variational
  literature).

## How to run

```bash
# Requires: nougat-ocr installed, PyTorch, ~5 GB GPU.
pip install nougat-ocr
nougat 1901.01234v2.pdf -o extraction/  --recompute
mv extraction/1901.01234v2.mmd extraction/nougat.mmd
```

Then diff the produced `nougat.mmd` against the equations quoted in
`report/REPORT.md` §1 to catch transcription errors.

**Not run in this backfill.** Method-accuracy claims in the report were
verified numerically; a Nougat pass is a nice-to-have documentation step, not
a scientific blocker.
